--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
About the original addon
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Lueur was created by Armytille and is published on CurseForge:

    https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/lueur
    CurseForge project ID 1732324

As of the 1.4.0 release (2026-10-21), the upstream project states no license:

  - the CurseForge "license" field is empty;
  - the distributed 1.4.0 archive contains no LICENSE or README file;
  - Lueur.toc carries no Author or license field;
  - no source comments mention a license.

This file is therefore NOT a grant of rights over Armytille's work, and it does
not restate or reinterpret theirs. Under ordinary copyright rules, code with no
declared license is "all rights reserved". If you want to reuse, redistribute or
build on Lueur itself, ask the author.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
What this license covers
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Everything in this project that is our own work is released under the MIT
License below. "Our own work" is the Simplified Chinese localization by
骑人知福-正直, and it means, in practice:

  - Locales/zhCN.lua        -- the Simplified Chinese text and command aliases;
  - the zhCN entries added to Nodes.lua (Simplified Chinese vein names);
  - the `zh` addition to the language list of deDE, enUS, esES, frFR and ruRU;
  - the `## Notes-zhCN` and `## Title-zhCN` lines in Lueur.toc;
  - NOTICE.md, and the documentation in this repository.

It does NOT cover the original addon code, its name, its icon, or the artwork
under Media/ -- those remain the property of their author.

